00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.740
Where does your journey start?

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.810
Every AI development
journey has to start

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:37.890
with a business scenario.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:41.910
In our case, we're going to talk
about a retailer called Zava.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.950
Zava is a fictitious enterprise
retailer selling home

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.040
improvement goods to DIY
project enthusiasts.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.490
And you are part of the
AI development team.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:53.250
You are tasked to build Cora,
an AI shopping assistant

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.910
that can answer customer
questions in store or online

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.740
and provide customer service.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.340
Now, you want to design Cora
to be friendly, helpful,

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.260
and cost-effective to deploy.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.840
But you also understand that in
this fast-paced environment,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.200
your agent needs to keep
adapting to changing conditions,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.410
changing systems,
and changing needs.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.570
So what do you do?

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:16.890
Well, let's start first

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:20.460
by understanding what AI
app development looks like.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.870
So at a very basic level, an
AI app is nothing but a model

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:28.530
that takes an incoming prompt,
does some processing on it

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.120
and generates a response.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.180
That response can then be used
to trigger other actions,

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.610
which in turn may generate
new prompts and so on

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.470
and the cycle continues.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.420
And that's at a very,
very basic level.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.280
You can think of this as
a monolithic application

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.070
where in order for that model
to generate that response,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.470
there's other things that
happened to coordinate it.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.870
But when we think about
scale level delivery,

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.130
it becomes more complicated.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.500
Now you have multiple
models, multiple prompts,

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.170
multiple conversations,
and you need to coordinate

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.820
and orchestrate all
these together.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.340
Plus now you need to
extract information

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.380
from all these
conversations at scale

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.000
to determine what
you need to do next.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.040
And that is a challenge.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.340
So traditional AI application
that's monolithic can't really

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.980
do this in a very agile way.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.110
This is where agents can help.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.660
Agent AI brings a
microservices-based approach

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.970
where every agent is
a single unit of work

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.340
that can be evolved
independently without having

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.140
to rewrite the entire system.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.870
What that means is now when
you have a giant application,

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:31.740
you can just go in and update
or evolve individual agents

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:32.820
without having to think

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.660
about how the entire application
has to be redeployed.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:41.280
But to do this, you need a
repeatable and simple way.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.970
And what we want to do is
talk to you about an analogy.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:48.570
You need a test kitchen where
you can quickly prototype

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:52.620
out these little agents before
you put them into production.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.240
And that's the analogy
we're using today.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.790
How do you go from
test kitchen to table?

00:02:56.790 --> 00:03:00.030
Think about your AI application
or your AI solution

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.450
as the equivalent of a
multi-course dinner menu

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.850
at a very popular restaurant.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:08.250
You don't go around
designing your recipes right

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.310
at the dinner table,
rather, test chefs, I mean,

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.230
great chefs will
have a test kitchen

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.540
where they quickly experiment
with these recipes

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.590
until they get something

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.710
that passes their taste
test or evaluation.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.420
Then they can take
those and move it

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:22.980
into their restaurant kitchen

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:27.810
or code-first development
environment to make that better.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.510
Today, we're going to see how
Microsoft Foundry portal is your

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.500
test kitchen.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.590
You can go rapidly from a
plan to a basic prototype

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.800
until your recipe works
without writing a single line

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.720
of code all in your browser.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.930
So what can Foundry do for you?

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.040
Let's think about it in terms

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.200
of three developer
needs that we need.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.780
First, when building
these agents

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:52.770
in a microservices approach,
we need to rapidly prototype,

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:57.660
build, and deploy them so we can
actually have real customers try

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:58.890
them out.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:01.200
Next, we understand that
things will change.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.230
Models may change, your prompt
requirements may change,

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.300
your situation that the
environment you are

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.040
in may change.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.860
We need ways to do easy
experimentation and evaluation

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.560
to test these prompts, models,
and datasets without having

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.300
to reprovision each time.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:18.450
And last but not least, your
app has to be trustworthy.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.250
We need mechanisms
for secure, scalable,

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.010
and production-ready
development.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.440
And that means having a
unified end-to-end platform

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.510
that provides all these
capabilities for us.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.390
So I want to hand off to my
colleague to see how we go

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.100
about actually building this.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:32.730
Carlotta.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.500
CARLOTTA CASTELLUCCIO:
Yeah, thanks Nitya.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:39.870
So yes, let's go deeper into how
Microsoft Foundry can help you

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:44.610
in this end-to-end journey that
Nitya kind of introduced to us

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.520
and how it's able to address
the developer needs we have

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.540
just seen.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.940
So first of all,
Microsoft Foundry,

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:55.710
you can orchestrate a
multi-agent system with support

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.700
of both interoperability
and also open frameworks.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.790
You can also access to
the best foundational

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:06.420
and open-source models
in the model catalog

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.840
and select the final model

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.570
which is the best fit
for your use case.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:15.030
You can connect your
AI apps and agents

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.740
to different knowledge sources

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.310
and tools using also
built-in features in order

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:25.500
to contextualize AI responses
and enable AI to take actions

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.750
on behalf of the user.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.750
You can continuously
evaluate your solution

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:33.810
through every stage of the
AI development lifecycle

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:37.140
with proper content safety and
security measures included

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:42.420
in every layer of your
AI app or your AI agent.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.210
Also, AI apps and
agents should be tuned

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:49.530
and customized continuously
to fit the business needs.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.390
And finally, you
need the ability

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:53.610
to deploy anywhere you want,

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:57.270
including to local
and edge devices.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:00.090
Now, we're not going to
see everything, of course,

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:03.810
in this session, but
at least most of it.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:07.590
The green points you see in
