00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:21.270
Now, basically, all you need

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:26.850
to get started is what Nitya
called a test kitchen,

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:31.410
where you can try out
various recipes to build new

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:35.250
and optimize existing AI
agents before deploying them

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.480
into production.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:40.620
And our test kitchen is the
Microsoft Foundry portal.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.100
Now, the Microsoft Foundry
portal provides a low-code

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.920
solution to this problem.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.770
Within the Microsoft Foundry
portal, you can experiment

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:53.490
with models, tools, and
instruction for a single agent

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:56.850
in a browser-based playground
before even writing a single

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.320
line of code.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.500
You can use built-in
support for observability.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:07.080
We are going to see phases,
evaluations, monitoring features

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.190
to accelerate the inner-outer
loop transitions iterating

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:12.870
quickly and deploying versions

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.500
that can be compared
in real time.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.680
You can then move seamlessly
to code-first environments

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:22.020
to transition to
multi-agent solution

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:25.890
or develop further customization

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:30.750
and use maybe more complex
frameworks and workflows.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:36.960
So you basically move from the
test kitchen to the restaurant.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.720
And it's never been
easier to build, optimize

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:44.190
and govern AI apps and agent
within a unified platform

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:47.520
as Microsoft Foundry portal.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:51.390
Now, looking at this
end-to-end developer journey,

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:54.330
the Foundry portal has been
kind of structured in a way

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:59.070
to mimic the three main phases
of this AI development journey.

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:01.770
So for each step, you
have the features

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.200
and the tools you
need to go for them.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:09.120
So in the design phase, you
identify the business use case,

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.230
you do model exploration,
you test your domain prompts

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:15.900
over different models
for comparison,

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:19.080
and you build your agent
prototype by keeping it

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.870
with the right tools
and knowledge.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.610
While you do that,
you should make sure

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:27.480
to have a robust tracing system
so you can debug your system,

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.850
inspect any issues,
and address them

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:33.450
with further fine tuning
and customization.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.910
Once you've got your
prototype ready,

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:40.140
you then can optimize it
further by moving into code,

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:43.050
hosting it maybe in
a dev container,

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:47.970
evaluating the overall agent
behavior, and publish it.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:50.790
Now, every time you complete
one of these steps,

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:53.070
like the build step or
the optimized step,

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:56.850
you should ask yourself if
what you have got is ready

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:58.620
to move to the next phase.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:03.810
So you're kind of satisfied with
the result so far by looking

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.140
at traces, looking at
evaluation results,

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:09.930
and specific metrics you define.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.540
Third step is about governance,

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:16.110
safety and application
integration and shipping.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:20.370
So making sure that your
application is ready

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:24.120
for production and you also
have everything you need

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:29.670
to monitor any
regression over time.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:32.160
All this process is a loop,

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:35.280
is an iterative process,
not a linear process.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:40.050
So you might need to go from
right to left at some point

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:43.860
because you need maybe further
customization of your model

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:48.600
or further customization of your
prompts or your overall agent.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.870
You need to run
evaluations once again.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:57.210
So again, it's a loop, it's an
iteration, an iterative process

00:09:57.210 --> 00:10:00.660
of continuous improvement
of your application.

