01:08:37.200 --> 01:08:38.670
But while we're here, let's talk

01:08:38.670 --> 01:08:40.730
about one last thing,
which is monitoring.

01:08:40.730 --> 01:08:42.740
So when you think about
observability, you're thinking

01:08:42.740 --> 01:08:44.420
about traces, monitoring,
and evaluation.

01:08:44.420 --> 01:08:49.040
Traces are kind of allowing you
to see the execution of a call.

01:08:49.040 --> 01:08:49.880
And evaluation is

01:08:49.880 --> 01:08:53.480
about assessing how well
your responses meet criteria

01:08:53.480 --> 01:08:55.340
for quality, safety, et cetera.

01:08:55.340 --> 01:08:58.310
But monitoring is how
you kind of get metrics

01:08:58.310 --> 01:09:02.030
from your production or usage of
the agent and understand things

01:09:02.030 --> 01:09:04.820
like what are the total number
of calls, what was the cost,

01:09:04.820 --> 01:09:05.750
what was the token usage,

01:09:05.750 --> 01:09:08.060
how many failures did
I have, and so on.

01:09:08.060 --> 01:09:10.880
So these are like operational
metrics that you see here,

01:09:10.880 --> 01:09:12.650
and they give you a
really good sense

01:09:12.650 --> 01:09:15.900
of what this
specific agent does.

01:09:15.900 --> 01:09:17.640
But there's more.

01:09:17.640 --> 01:09:20.280
Remember, this is a single
agent, this is a microservice,

01:09:20.280 --> 01:09:23.520
